WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
Hello everybody my name is Markiplier and welcome back to Doki Doki Literature Club!

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:09.560
Okay! Alright! Everybody hold onto your horses 'cause I got the poem of your dreams right here.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.880
Alright, who do I show it to first?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.200
Hey Monika!

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.960
EEEEEY Monika baby!

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.700
Hang on I better save on this one.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.240
It's a genius poem. Can't let the genius go to -- HEY Monika!

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.300
Hey come here!

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.440
I should start with Monika.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.920
Yesterday she seemed eager to read my poem and I want her to know I'm putting in effort.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.060
Puttin' in effort, Monika!

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.680
"Hi, Morp!"

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:33.880
Hi, Monika.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.880
"Having a good time so far?"

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.220
Sure, okay.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.380
Ah... yeah. "Good, glad to hear it!"

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.300
"By the way, since you're new and everything..

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.200
If you ever have any suggestions for the club, like new activities or things we can do better..

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.440
I'm always listening!"

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.920
And then I'll ignore you. And punch you in the face for daring to change my beautiful club.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.120
"Don't be afraid to bring things up, okay?"

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.200
Alright, I'll keep that in mind.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.300
Of course I'll be afraid to bring things up.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.320
I'm much better off just going with the flow until I'm more settled in.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.880
"AAAAAnyway.."

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.880
"Wanna share your poem with me?"

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.880
It's kind of embarrassing but I guess I have to.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.520
"aHAHAhahaHahahAHA!"

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.500
"Don't worry, Morp. We're all a little embarrassed today, you know?"

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.360
You know, I don't trust you.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:13.360
But that's okay.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.740
"But it's the sort of barrier that we'll all learn to get past soon."

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.880
Yea, that's true.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.400
I hand Monika my poem.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.420
"...Mhm. Great job, Morp!"

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.120
"I was going 'OoOoh' in my head while reading it."

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.140
Not out loud though, I would never do that.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.800
"It's really metaphorical."

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.120
"I'm not sure why but I didn't expect you to go for something so deep."

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.840
"I guess I underestimated you."

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.840
Hey! Sure! Was it the vivacious?

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.620
It was probably the vivacious.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:39.920
It's easiest for me to keep everyone's expectations low.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.320
That way it always counts when I put in some effort.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.000
"HA! That's not very fair."

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.980
"Well, I guess it worked out anyway."

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.620
"You know that Yuri likes this kind of writing, right?"

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.100
"Writing that's full of imagery and symbolism."

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:56.500
"Unlike Sayori, who likes simple and direct words to describe happiness and sadness."

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.000
"Yuri likes when readers are left to derive their own meaning out of it."

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.500
"It's very challenging to write like that effectively."

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.360
"Both allowing people to get something out of it just by feel..

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.280
Or letting them deeply analyze all of the nuances."

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.960
"It can take years of practice-- which I'm assuming Yuri has at this point."

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:15.640
I never really asked though, I'm sure I'm nowhere NEAR her level yet.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.340
"Ah, don't worry so much about that."

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.900
"You do your own thing."

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.640
"Just keep exploring and learn by trying new things."

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.180
I'm sure I'll end up trying different things a lot!

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.820
It could take a while before I'd feel comfortable doing this.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.880
"That's okay!"

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.720
"I'd love to see you try new things."

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.420
"That's the best way to find the kind of style that suits you!"

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.620
"Everyone else might be a little bit biased towards their own kinds of styles..

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.340
But I'll always help you find what suits you the most."

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.240
"So don't force yourself to write the way everyone else wants you to write."

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.780
"It's not like you have to worry about impressing them or anything."

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.520
"Ahaha!" Okay, I don't like this.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.180
"Anyway, you- you want to read my poem now?"

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:51.800
"Don't worry, I'm not very good."

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.500
You sound pretty confident for someone who claims to not be very good.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.640
"Well, that's 'cuz I have to sound confident."

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.260
"That doesn't mean I always feel that way, you know."

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.240
I see.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.000
Well, let's read it, then.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:02.940
Ah.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.820
"Hole in the Wall"

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:05.860
"It couldn't-"

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.340
What kind of hole are we talking about?

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.480
"It couldn't have been me.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.080
See, the direction the spackle protrudes.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.400
A noisy neighbor?

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.820
An angry boyfriend?

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.820
I'll never know. I wasn't home.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.860
I peer inside for a clue.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:22.640
No! I can't see. I reel, blind, like a film left out in the sun.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.660
But it's too late. My retinas.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.280
Already scorched with a permanent copy of the meaningless image.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.900
It's just a little hole. It wasn't too bright.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:31.960
It was too deep.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.000
Stretching forever into everything.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.120
A hole of infinite choices

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.320
I realize now that I wasn't looking in

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.720
I was looking out.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.280
And he, on the other side, was looking in."

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:44.800
Beautiful.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.520
"So what do you think?"

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.120
Oh! [kissing noise]

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.380
I've never been so excited about a hole in my life!

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.280
Oh it's a beautiful thing!

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.960
Hmm. It's very freeform, if that's what you'd call it.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.200
Sorry, I'm not really the right person to ask for feedback.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.800
"Hahaha, it's okay."

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.400
"Yeah, that kind of style has gotten pretty popular nowadays."

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.580
"That is, a lot of poems have been putting emphasis on the timing between words and lines."

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.800
"When performed out loud, it can be really powerful."

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.200
What was the inspiration behind this one?

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.900
"Ah. Well, I'm not sure if I know how to put it."

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.580
"I guess you could say that I had some kind of epiphany recently."

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:18.440
"It's been influencing my poems a bit."

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.480
An epiphany?

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.840
"Yeah, something like that."

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.800
"I'm kinda nervous to talk about deep stuff like that because it's kind of coming on strongly."

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.120
"Maybe after everyone is better friends with each other."

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.720
"Anyway. Here's Monika's writing tip of the day!"

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:34.300
"Sometimes when you're writing a poem or story, your brain gets too fixated on a specific point."

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.640
"If you try so hard to make it perfect, then you'll never make any progress."

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:40.820
"Just force yourself to get something down on paper, and tidy it up later."

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.820
"Another way to think about it is this."

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.820
"If you keep your pen in the same spot for too long, you'll just get a big dark puddle of ink."

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.820
"So just move your hand and go with the flow."

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.340
"That's my advice for the day."

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.200
"Thanks for listening~"

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:56.000
Alright. Cool. Alright. Who should I show my poem to next?

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.960
I don't know... I don't...

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.200
How about no one?

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.760
Oh NatSUUKII!

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.120
Sayooori?

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.040
Natsuki. I haven't talked to you yet.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.460
Eeeey, waddup?

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.540
"Well, it's about what I expected from someone like you."

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.800
What?! Excuse you!

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.080
That's a little blunt.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.500
"Well, excuse me."

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.900
"It's not like I said that was bad."

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.000
"It just didn't evoke any emotions."

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.300
So basically it's not cute enough for your tastes?

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.920
"Do you want to get smacked?"

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:25.880
I'll pass.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.780
"*sigh*"

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.060
"Well anyway, I guess I need to show you mine."

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:30.740
"Not that you'll like it."

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:32.040
"Eagles Can Fly"

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.320
"Monkeys can climb

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.520
Crickets can leap

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.760
Horses can race

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.020
Owls can seek

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.260
Cheetahs can run

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.480
Eagles can fly

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.840
People can try

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.340
But that's a-bout it."

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.540
Aw, that's beautiful!

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:46.960
That's beautiful!

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:48.480
I like it.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.140
I really like it! I actually like it.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:51.720
"I told you that you weren't going to like it."

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.800
I like it!

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:53.580
"What?"

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.520
"Just be honest!"

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.180
I am.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.300
Why are you so convinced that I wouldn't like it?

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.600
"WELL-"

00:05:58.600 --> 00:05:59.580
UUUHHH-

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.760
"Because!"

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:04.480
"Everyone in high school thinks that writing has to be all sophisticated and stuff."

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.000
"So people don't even take my writing seriously."

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.340
But isn't the point of poems for people to express themselves?"

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.300
Your writing style wouldn't make your message any less valid.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.440
"Yeah! Exactly!"

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.080
"I like it when it's easy to read but it hits you hard."

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.300
"Like in this poem."

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.560
"Seeing everyone around you do great things can be really disheartening..

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.480
So I decided to write about it."

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.900
Yeah, I understand.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:29.640
"But the other nice thing about simple writing is that it puts more weight on the wordplay."

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:34.220
"Like I set up for a rhyme at the end, but then made it fall flat on purpose."

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.260
"It helps bring out the feeling in the last line."

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.360
So you did.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.920
I guess more went into it than I realized.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.500
"That's what it means to be a pro!"

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:44.940
"I'm glad you learned something."

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.400
"Didn't expect that from the youngest one here, did you?"

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.700
Yeah, I guess not.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:51.120
I decide to humor her with the last comment.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.080
I don't really care how old everyone is, but if Natsuki is feeling proud then I won't take that away from her.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:57.160
Aw.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.520
How about Sayori? Sayori!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.920
Hey Sayooori!

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.100
SaYaOwori!

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:04.520
"This is a good poem, Morp!"

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.000
"Are you sure it's your first time?"

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:06.920
Of course!

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.160
It's not that good.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.200
Am I the kind of guy who would be writing poems in his spare time?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.560
"Hehe, I guess you're right."

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:13.700
"You're pretty terrible."

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.100
"But that's why it impressed me!"

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.120
"Well, to be honest..

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.000
I was afraid that you wouldn't do it seriously."

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.840
"Or that you wouldn't write one at all."

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.560
"I'm really happy just that you wrote one."

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:24.200
"It reminds me of how you really are part of the club now."

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.600
Not to mention the fact that I'm standing in front of you in the club room?

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:27.860
Eh, well of course.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.920
I'm not really into it yet, but that doesn't mean I'll break my promise.

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:31.640
"See?"

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.180
"It's like I said before, Morp..

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.480
Deep down, you're not selfish at all, you know?"

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.080
That's a backhanded compliment...

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.980
"Trying new things like this for other people..

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:40.980
That's something that only really good people do."

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.260
Thanks... I guess.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.940
I'm not sure if Sayori sees the full picture of my motive here.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.820
Then again, I can't deny that she's part of the reason I joined.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.780
Knowing how much this means to her and all.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.300
Yeah...

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.880
"and I'm gonna make sure you have lots of fun here, okay?"

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.720
Oh! Yeah alright.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:07.280
Hang on, wait. I gotta save again. I don't know why, I just gotta save.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.840
[laughs]

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:39.800
[laughs again]

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.400
I-- I-- sure. Okay.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.520
I can't really see you as being cranky anyway.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.200
You got it Sayori.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.960
Huh. Interesting.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.880
Alright well it's just Yuri left.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:41.640
This hasn't taken a dark turn yet, but I got a funny feeling about it.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.600
Ugh. Her mouth just grows exponentially and she has to keep that shit contained.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.560
You've got great thumbs after all.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.560
Alright so you're a ghost, is that what you're saying?

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:41.320
Your're a ghost. I get it, I see it ghost girl. Okay. I know. I get it.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:52.840
Ah Morp very stupid! You need to understand this about Morp.

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:54.760
Morp very a dummy.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:04.040
Eh?

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.360
blooh! [weird mouth noises]

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.200
Are you a ghost?

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.200
Your thumb felt very solid.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.480
Your thumbs...

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.000
You got real teaching thumbs.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.160
Okay! Alright.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:51.240
Morp liked it! Morp liked it a lot!

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.200
Which yours was not.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:28.880
[orgasm/mouth sound]

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:31.280
[weird sound]

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:33.960
[continues making odd noises that may be confused with certain sexual sounds]

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:40.920
[throat sound resembling "huh?!"]

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:48.080
UUGH! EEIY!

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.680
[sound resembling a deep screaming sheep]

00:16:57.760 --> 00:16:58.400
[laughs]

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.040
Uh-- wha--? Natsuki!

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:27.620
My boobs have been the same size!

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:28.600
DDUUUR!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:31.360
Hang on, I just gotta save. There's conflict here.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:08.400
UUGH! UUUH? UUuUuUGH?!

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.680
Oh! Oh boy! Okay, conflict! Hang on.

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.560
Alright, I gotta think about his one.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:22.360
Uh.

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:24.240
Put on my thinking pants!

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:26.000
Oh wait I'm not wearing pants...

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:26.800
MREH.

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:28.200
MMH.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:30.400
Mm.

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:35.960
M.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.280
NNAlright okay alright. Well.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.880
Okay well Yuri's full of herself.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.600
Yuri's full of herself. She's being a little uppity.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.720
Being a little up... itty...

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.960
Natsuki was defensive off the bat...

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:56.040
But Yuri was dismissive off the bat. That's the two juxtapositions here.

00:18:56.040 --> 00:19:02.080
Like, neither of them were right. I mean they're right in their own ways but obviously I can't take a side on it.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:04.560
Maybe Sayori can help me...

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:05.120
Sayori!

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:06.320
Help! Please!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:07.160
Heeelp!

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:10.480
Help! I really don't care what their opinions of me are!

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:20.120
UUURF. UGH.

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:39.640
Be-- Because Morp's so hot!

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:49.640
[laughs]

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.080
Big and beautiful!

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.320
Oh! Monika!

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:47.800
Why do I have a funny feeling this is going to take a horrifying turn?

